{"id":"rp2047-5","designation":"RP 2047-5","title":"Carriage of VC-2 Compressed Video — VC-2 Level 66 Compression of Ultra-High Definition Video Sources for Use with a High Definition Infrastructure","state":"active","suite":"2047","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/rp2047-5/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/rp2047-5/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"This Recommended Practice defines constraints on the VC-2 video compression specification such that 10-bit ultra-high definition video signals can be compressed to only occupy the bit rate of 8-bit high definition signals. Specifically, it defines constraints for compressing progressive source video having 3840 pixels/line by 2160 lines/frame at 50 or 60/1.001 frames/s using 4:2:2 sampling. This document defines a VC-2 bitstream for video compressed according to this Recommended Practice. It also defines an application-specific level for VC-2 compression.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"Foreword","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"Introduction","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"2 Normative References","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"3 Terms and Definitions","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"4 Overview (informative)","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"5 General","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"6 Coding Constraints","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 Overview (informative)","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 Video Source parameters","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"6.3 Coding parameters","page":5},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.1 Profile and syntax","page":5},{"level":4,"title":"6.3.1.1 General","page":5},{"level":4,"title":"6.3.1.2 Parse parameters","page":5},{"level":4,"title":"6.3.1.3 Base video format","page":5},{"level":4,"title":"6.3.1.4 Source parameters","page":5},{"level":4,"title":"6.3.1.5 Picture Coding Mode","page":6},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.2 Picture syntax","page":6},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.3 Transform parameters","page":6},{"level":4,"title":"6.3.3.1 Wavelet filter","pag